SECTION 1 — ELEMENTARY CELLULAR AUTOMATON (ECA)
----------------------------------------------------------------------
Model:
    • 1D lattice of width W (e.g., 201 cells)
    • Binary alphabet {0,1}
    • Neighborhood: (left, center, right)
    • Rule: integer R ∈ [0,255]
    • Rule encoded as 8-bit binary:
          bit 7 → neighborhood 111
          bit 6 → neighborhood 110
          ...
          bit 0 → neighborhood 000

Code:
    - Converts rule number → binary string → lookup table.
    - Uses:
          neighborhoods = 4*L + 2*C + R
      where L,C,R are the left/center/right bits.
    - Next state:
          next[i] = rule_bin[7 - neighborhoods[i]]

Initial conditions:
    • "single" → one 1 in the center
    • "random" → random 0/1 array

History:
    • history[t] = state at time t
    • shape = (steps, width)

